            <title>[LU-21266] o2iblnd: NULL list_del in kiblnd_destroy_tx_pool after ENOMEM</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21266</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;An allocation failure in &lt;tt&gt;kiblnd_create_tx_pool()&lt;/tt&gt; makes &lt;tt&gt;kiblnd_destroy_tx_pool()&lt;/tt&gt; dereference a NULL pointer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Mechanism"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Mechanism&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;kiblnd_create_tx_pool()&lt;/tt&gt; zeroes all &lt;tt&gt;tpo_tx_descs&lt;/tt&gt; with &lt;tt&gt;memset()&lt;/tt&gt;. It then allocates the per-tx arrays in a loop. On an allocation failure, the loop stops with &lt;tt&gt;break&lt;/tt&gt;, and the function calls &lt;tt&gt;ps-&amp;gt;ps_pool_destroy()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;kiblnd_destroy_tx_pool()&lt;/tt&gt; calls &lt;tt&gt;list_del(&amp;amp;tx-&amp;gt;tx_list)&lt;/tt&gt; for each of the &lt;tt&gt;po_size&lt;/tt&gt; descriptors. Only &lt;tt&gt;kiblnd_map_tx_pool()&lt;/tt&gt; adds a descriptor to &lt;tt&gt;po_free_list&lt;/tt&gt;, and the create function calls it only after the loop completes. On the failure path, every &lt;tt&gt;tx_list&lt;/tt&gt; is still zero. &lt;tt&gt;list_del()&lt;/tt&gt; then writes through a NULL &lt;tt&gt;next&lt;/tt&gt; pointer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;kiblnd_create_tx_pool()
  memset(tpo-&amp;gt;tpo_tx_descs, 0, ...)
  &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (i = 0; i &amp;lt; size; i++)
      LIBCFS_CPT_ALLOC(...) fails -&amp;gt; &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;break&lt;/span&gt;
  ps-&amp;gt;ps_pool_destroy(pool)
    kiblnd_destroy_tx_pool()
      list_del(&amp;amp;tx-&amp;gt;tx_list)   &amp;lt;- tx_list.next == NULL
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Trigger"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Trigger&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any of the per-tx allocations (&lt;tt&gt;tx_pages&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;tx_frags&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;tx_wrq&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;tx_sge&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;tx_rd&lt;/tt&gt;) fails under memory pressure. The failure can happen at LNet startup or when the pool set grows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Initialize &lt;tt&gt;tx_list&lt;/tt&gt; of each descriptor before the allocation loop, so that &lt;tt&gt;list_del()&lt;/tt&gt; is safe on the failure path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The defect is source-only. Nobody has seen the crash in a log. A code review found the defect on current master.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
